---
import TutorialLayout from '../../../layouts/TutorialLayout.astro';
import ModelWorkbench from '../../../components/tutorials/ModelWorkbench';
import MathBlock from '../../../components/common/MathBlock.astro';
---

<TutorialLayout
  title="Your First Model"
  breadcrumbs={[
    { label: 'Tutorials', href: '/tutorials' },
    { label: 'Getting Started', href: '/tutorials/getting-started' },
    { label: 'Your First Model' },
  ]}
  next={{ label: 'Mass-Spring-Damper', href: '/tutorials/getting-started/mass-spring-damper' }}
>
  <div class="mb-6 p-4 rounded-lg border border-accent/20 bg-accent/5">
    <h3 class="text-sm font-semibold text-accent mb-2">What you'll learn</h3>
    <ul class="list-disc list-inside text-sm text-text-muted space-y-1">
      <li>Simulation workflow: write Modelica, simulate, and plot results</li>
      <li>How to read a second-order ODE in Modelica syntax</li>
      <li>How to interact with the simulation workbench</li>
    </ul>
  </div>

  <p class="text-text-muted leading-relaxed mb-4">
    Welcome to Rumoca. In this tutorial you will write a Modelica model, simulate it, and explore the
    results &mdash; all in your browser. No install required.
  </p>

  <p class="text-text-muted leading-relaxed mb-4">
    We will start with the <strong class="text-text">double integrator</strong> &mdash; the simplest second-order
    ODE. A constant acceleration <em>a</em> drives velocity <em>v</em>, which drives position <em>x</em>:
  </p>

  <MathBlock tex={`\\begin{aligned}
\\frac{dx}{dt} &= v \\\\
\\frac{dv}{dt} &= a
\\end{aligned}`} />

  <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-text mb-3">Try it</h2>
  <p class="text-text-muted leading-relaxed mb-4">
    The editor below contains a complete Modelica model. Click <strong class="text-text">Simulate</strong> to
    run 5 seconds of integration. Toggle variables in the plot legend to explore the results.
  </p>

  <ModelWorkbench
    client:only="react"
    initialSource={`model DoubleIntegrator "Double integrator (constant acceleration)"
  parameter Real a = 1.0 "Constant acceleration (m/s^2)";
  Real x(start = 0.0) "Position (m)";
  Real v(start = 0.0) "Velocity (m/s)";
equation
  der(x) = v;
  der(v) = a;
end DoubleIntegrator;`}
    modelName="DoubleIntegrator"
    tEnd={5}
  />

  <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-text mt-10 mb-3">What just happened?</h2>
  <ol class="list-decimal list-inside text-text-muted leading-relaxed space-y-2 mb-6">
    <li><strong class="text-text">Simulate</strong> &mdash; Rumoca parsed your Modelica source and integrated the ODE in your browser using WebAssembly. No server round-trip.</li>
    <li><strong class="text-text">Plot</strong> &mdash; State trajectories are plotted over time. Position <em>x</em> grows quadratically; velocity <em>v</em> grows linearly.</li>
  </ol>


  <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-text mt-10 mb-3">Things to try</h2>
  <ul class="list-disc list-inside text-text-muted leading-relaxed space-y-2 mb-6">
    <li>Change the acceleration <code class="font-mono text-sm text-accent">a</code> to <code class="font-mono text-sm text-accent">-9.81</code> and re-simulate &mdash; you now have free-fall under gravity.</li>
    <li>Give the ball an initial velocity by changing <code class="font-mono text-sm text-accent">v(start&nbsp;=&nbsp;0.0)</code> to <code class="font-mono text-sm text-accent">v(start&nbsp;=&nbsp;5.0)</code>.</li>
    <li>Increase the simulation time to see how the trajectories extend.</li>
  </ul>
</TutorialLayout>
